    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: SBQQ__ContractedPrice__c records that are expired, point to inactive products, or have zero/null prices.
Why it matters: Stale contracted prices either keep overriding standard pricing (locked-in low prices that should have rolled off — direct revenue leakage) or fail to apply at all when reps expect them. Both cause customer disputes.
Suppress a finding: when a contract is intentionally held open at $0 as a contractual placeholder pending true-up.
Disable the detector: only if your org doesn&apos;t use SBQQ__ContractedPrice__c. Most CPQ orgs should leave this on.</value></values>
